# DipTrace design files are binary containers (the PCB layouts start with a
# "DTBOARD" magic). Marking them `binary` is shorthand for -diff -merge -text:
# git stops trying to produce a textual diff, stops line-merging them — which
# would silently corrupt a layout — and never rewrites line endings inside them.
#
# The practical consequence: these files cannot be merged. Two people editing
# the same board in parallel means one of the two versions is lost, so treat a
# board file as checked out by one person at a time.
*.dip  binary
*.dch  binary
